###The instruction to evaluate:
Evaluate the coherence and logical flow of the following {{ domain_format }}. Consider three distinct aspects:
- Connectivity: Whether individual sentences and ideas link to each other through clear transitions, consistent references, or explicit logical connectors. Flag missing transitions, ambiguous pronoun or noun-phrase references, or implicit logical jumps the reader must supply.
- Progression: Whether the sequence of ideas reflects a structured, purposeful order -- either following the source's own logic or a defensible alternative structure (e.g., most-important-first).
- Unity: Whether the {{ domain_format }} reads as a single coherent piece rather than a set of loosely assembled statements. Flag cases where the {{ domain_format }} lacks a discernible through-line, or shifts register or focus without justification.

Boundary note: Do not deduct for grammatical awkwardness or phrasing style -- those belong to the fluency dimension. However, if syntactic confusion directly creates a logical gap (i.e., the reader cannot determine what a sentence is asserting or how it connects to the next), treat this as a connectivity failure and apply the deduction here. Note the overlap explicitly in your feedback.

